  "description": "BIBCAT crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H63 Dy5 N16 O26 P2,C70 H67 Dy5 N16 O26 P2,2(C1 H1 Cl3). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.818-4.177 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.69-118.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C140H132Dy10N32O52P4Cl6.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
